{% extends 'pages/communities/sagamok/members-first-plan-layout.html.twig' %}
{% set plan_key = 'wealth' %}{% set plan_short = 'Community wealth' %}{% set plan_eyebrow = 'Priority 2' %}
{% set plan_title = 'Protect and grow community wealth' %}
{% set plan_description = 'Give members one clear account of the settlement trust, debt, company lending, investment returns, withdrawals and benefits reaching the community.' %}
{% block plan_content %}
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">The outcome</p><h2>Every dollar has a purpose, an authority, a risk limit and a reported result.</h2><p class="plan-lede">The trust protects future generations while supporting disciplined Nation-building today. Borrowing and internal lending remain visible beside the assets they finance.</p></header><div class="plan-grid plan-grid--3"><div class="plan-card"><h3>Protect principal</h3><p>Set a member-approved floor, withdrawal rules and a long-term return objective.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>See the whole balance sheet</h3><p>Report trust assets, Nation debt, guarantees and company receivables together.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Trace member benefit</h3><p>Connect each use of capital to jobs, homes, services, repayments or durable assets.</p></div></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Public baseline</p><h2>The scale requires a single reconciliation.</h2></header><div class="plan-grid plan-grid--3"><div class="plan-card"><h3>$219,001,971</h3><p>Trust market value reported at December 31, 2025.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>$96,972,955</h3><p>Loans due from Government Business Enterprises at March 31, 2025.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>$100,516,135</h3><p>Long-term debt reported at March 31, 2025.</p></div></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Year One commitments</p><h2>Put the rules and reporting in place.</h2></header><div class="plan-commitments"><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Community wealth statement</h3><p>Reconcile opening balance, income, withdrawals, transfers, lending, debt, fees and closing balance.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Trust policy</h3><p>Publish the purpose, authorities, asset rules, risk limits, withdrawal test, conflicts and reporting duties.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Debt and guarantee register</h3><p>List lender, borrower, balance, rate, maturity, security, guarantee and repayment status.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Capital allocation framework</h3><p>Compare community infrastructure, services, liquidity and enterprise proposals using one scoring method.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Independent performance review</h3><p>Compare investment and borrowing results with the adopted benchmarks and risk limits.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Intergenerational report</h3><p>Show what is preserved, what is used now and the expected effect over ten and twenty years.</p></article></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Quarterly measures</p><h2>What members receive.</h2></header><div class="plan-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Report</th><th>Control</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Trust market value and return</td><td>Quarter and since inception</td><td>Compare with approved benchmark</td></tr><tr><td>Withdrawals and transfers</td><td>Amount, purpose and authority</td><td>Confirm policy test passed</td></tr><tr><td>Company-loan performance</td><td>Balance, rate, payments and arrears</td><td>Flag covenant or repayment changes</td></tr><tr><td>Total debt and guarantees</td><td>Opening, new, repaid and closing</td><td>Compare with affordability limit</td></tr><tr><td>Member benefit</td><td>Jobs, homes, services and distributions</td><td>State method and evidence</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="plan-decision"><h2>Decisions members make</h2><ul><li>What portion of wealth must remain protected?</li><li>Which uses require a direct member vote?</li><li>What return and risk limits govern enterprise lending?</li><li>How should benefits be balanced between current needs and future generations?</li></ul></section>
<div class="plan-next"><a href="/communities/sagamok/members-first-plan/member-government">← Member government</a><a href="/communities/sagamok/members-first-plan/enterprises">Next: Enterprises →</a></div>
{% endblock %}
